<title>TURKEY: Turk official say no Iraqi oil at Ceyhan so far.</title>
<headline>Turk official say no Iraqi oil at Ceyhan so far.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Turkish oil official said no Iraqi oil had arrived at a Turkish terminal on Tuesday, hours after Iraq said it had begun pumping crude exports from its northern city of Kirkuk.</p>
<p>&quot;No oil was pumped into Ceyhan today,&quot; Fatih Sen, a regional official of Turkey's state-owned Botas pipeline company, told Reuters. He said he had no information on a reported fault at the Kirkuk pumping station.</p>
</text>
